$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Welcome to THE TEMPLE OF HERMES"$$FG$

THE TEMPLE OF HERMES is a x86_64, multi-cored, non-preemptive multi-tasking,
ring-0-only, single-address mapped (identity-mapped), operating system for
recreational programming and for a human and an AI agent sharing one machine.
It is a rebrand and continuation of TinkerOS, which is a fork of TempleOS by
Terry A. Davis.  This image is version 0.1.0 and keeps the TempleOS API and
TinkerOS compatibility of its base.

The first terminal starts in USER mode and opens the $LK,"Start page",A="FI:::/Doc/Start.DD"$.
The Hermes daemon is already on COM1.  See $LK,"About THE TEMPLE OF HERMES",A="FI:::/Doc/AboutHermes.DD"$
and $LK,"Features",A="FI:::/Doc/Features.DD"$.

* See also the $FG,4$$TX,"TempleOS Welcome",HTML="https://tinkeros.github.io/WbTempleOS/Doc/Welcome.html"$$FG$

$FG,8$
